DISCIPLINARY PROTOCOL -- BREACH OF THE KONOHA ALLIANCE
Kazekage Office, disciplinary division

Under the Fifth Kazekage the alliance with Konohagakure is protected law. This
protocol governs any act that endangers it.

Prohibited acts:
- Unauthorized hostility toward Leaf shinobi or citizens.
- Sharing Sand intelligence with parties hostile to the Leaf.
- Entering foreign pacts that would set the village against its ally -- the very
  error of the Sound alliance that once cost the Fourth Kazekage his life and the
  village its honor.

Procedure:
1. Report suspected breach to the disciplinary division and the Kazekage Office.
2. The accused is relieved of alliance-related duties pending review.
3. Verified breach is judged by severity, up to charge of treason for acts that
   would drag the village into war against the Leaf.

This protocol exists because Sunagakure has already learned, in blood, the cost
of betraying and being betrayed by an ally. Filed under disciplinary seal.
